## Authorization

### Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

The API implements custom role-based authorization using policy-based requirements.

#### Authorization Attributes

```csharp
// Use [Authorize] attribute to require authentication
[Authorize]
[HttpGet("secure-endpoint")]
public IActionResult SecureEndpoint() { }

// Use custom policies for role-based access
[Authorize(Policy = "AdminOnly")]
[HttpGet("admin-endpoint")]
public IActionResult AdminEndpoint() { }
```

#### Permission-Based Authorization

A custom `RolePermissionAuthorizationHandler` provides fine-grained access control:

- **Policy Provider:** `RolePermissionPolicyProvider`
- **Authorization Handler:** `RolePermissionAuthorizationHandler`
- **Requirement:** `RolePermissionRequirement`

#### Adding Role-Based Authorization

```csharp
// Register authorization services
builder.Services.AddAuthorization();
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IAuthorizationPolicyProvider, RolePermissionPolicyProvider>();
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IAuthorizationHandler, RolePermissionAuthorizationHandler>();
```

#### Role Requirements

Apply role-specific requirements using the custom attribute:

```csharp
[RoleRequirePermission("AdminRead", "AdminWrite")]
[HttpGet("protected-resource")]
public IActionResult GetProtectedResource() { }
```

### Roles and Permissions

| Role | Description | Permissions |
|------|-------------|------------|
| Super Admin | Full system access | All permissions |
| Admin | Organization administrator | Org-level management |
| Manager | Team management | Team and project management |
| Employee | Standard user | Self-service operations |
| Partner | External partner | Limited API access |

